<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>High Tide Books // Financial Dashboard</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
    <style>
        /* Compact money tables: lots of columns, so tighten the global padding */
        .fin-table th, .fin-table td { padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        .fin-table th { letter-spacing: 1px; }
        .fin-table .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
        .fin-table th.num { text-align: right; }
        .fin-table .muted { color: #888; }
        .fin-table .sub { display: block; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #aaa; }
        .fin-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 30px; border-radius: 12px; }
        .fin-table input[type="number"] { width: 90px; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: right; }
        .fin-table button { padding: 6px 14px; font-size: 0.8rem; width: auto; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <a href="/admin"><- Back to Management</a>
            <h1 style="margin: 0;">High Tide Books: Business Plan 2026</h1>
        </div>

        <%
            // --- All figures below come from the same assumptions (see plan.*) ---
            const totalFixed = plan.rent + plan.utilities + plan.helpers + plan.ss_helpers + plan.autonomo + plan.misc;

            // Books: margin on the net price, i.e. after IVA has gone to Hacienda
            const bookProfit   = actualSales * plan.book_profit_rate;
            // Events: already priced and costed per event type in the database
            const ticketSales  = actualTicketSales;
            const ticketProfit = actualEventProfit;
            const totalProfit  = bookProfit + ticketProfit;
            const netResult    = totalProfit - totalFixed;

            // THE break-even target: one definition, reused everywhere on this page
            const breakEvenBooks   = Math.ceil(totalFixed / plan.profit_per_book);
            const breakEvenTickets = Math.ceil(totalFixed / plan.ref_event_profit);
            const missing          = Math.max(0, -netResult);
            const money = v => v.toFixed(2) + ' €';
        %>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 30px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            
        <!-- FIXED COSTS PANEL -->
            <div style="background: #fdfdfd; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 25px; border-radius: 12px;">
                <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--secondary); padding-bottom: 10px;">Monthly Fixed Costs (The "Burn")</h3>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; line-height: 2;">
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Shop Rent (Main Shop Center)</span> <strong><%= plan.rent.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Utilities (Elec/Water/WiFi)</span> <strong><%= plan.utilities.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Staff (3 Helpers @ 600€)</span> <strong><%= plan.helpers.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Social Security (Helpers 32%)</span> <strong><%= plan.ss_helpers.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Autónomo Fee (Owner)</span> <strong><%= plan.autonomo.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;"><span>Insurance & Misc</span> <strong><%= plan.misc.toFixed(2) %> €</strong></li>
                    <li style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 15px; border-top: 2px solid #ddd; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 1.2rem;">
                        <strong>Total Monthly Burn</strong> 
                        <strong style="color: var(--primary);"><%= totalFixed.toFixed(2) %> €</strong>
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 15px; border-top: 1px solid #eee; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666;">
                    <strong>Break-even target for this burn:</strong>
                    <%= breakEvenBooks %> books <em>or</em> <%= breakEvenTickets %> "<%= plan.ref_event_type %>" tickets per month
                    (any mix in between). At <%= plan.avg_book_price.toFixed(2) %> € a book you keep
                    <%= plan.profit_per_book.toFixed(2) %> €; a <%= plan.ref_event_price.toFixed(2) %> € ticket keeps
                    <%= plan.ref_event_profit.toFixed(2) %> €.
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- PERFORMANCE DASHBOARD -->
            <div style="background: #eff6f6; border: 1px solid var(--secondary); padding: 25px; border-radius: 12px;">
                <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--secondary); padding-bottom: 10px;">Current Month Real-time Performance</h3>
                
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                    <div style="flex: 1; background: #fff; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #ddd;">
                        <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888; text-transform: uppercase;">Book Sales</div>
                        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: bold;"><%= actualSales.toFixed(2) %> €</div>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);"><%= bookProfit.toFixed(2) %> € profit</div>
                    </div>
                    <div style="flex: 1; background: #fff; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #ddd;">
                        <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888; text-transform: uppercase;">Event Tickets</div>
                        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: bold;"><%= ticketSales.toFixed(2) %> €</div>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--secondary);"><%= ticketProfit.toFixed(2) %> € profit</div>
                        <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #aaa;"><%= actualTickets %> tickets across <%= actualEventCount %> events</div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #fff; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">
                    <h4 style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Monthly Balance</h4>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Profit books + events:</span>
                        <strong style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--secondary);"><%= totalProfit.toFixed(2) %> €</strong>
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-top: 6px;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.1rem;">- Monthly burn:</span>
                        <strong style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #888;"><%= totalFixed.toFixed(2) %> €</strong>
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 10px;">
                        <span style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Profit book shop:</span>
                        <strong style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: <%= netResult >= 0 ? 'var(--secondary)' : 'var(--accent)' %>;">
                            <%= netResult.toFixed(2) %> €
                        </strong>
                    </div>
                    
                    <% if (netResult < 0) { %>
                        <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding: 10px; background: #fdf6e3; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #eee8d5;">
                            <strong>Still missing <%= missing.toFixed(2) %> €</strong> to reach the break-even target of
                            <%= breakEvenBooks %> books / <%= breakEvenTickets %> tickets:
                            <%= Math.ceil(missing / plan.profit_per_book) %> more books <em>or</em>
                            <%= Math.ceil(missing / plan.ref_event_profit) %> more tickets this month.
                        </div>
                    <% } else { %>
                        <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding: 10px; background: #eff6f6; color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #d1e5e5;">
                            <strong>Break-even reached.</strong> Everything above covers the burn: <%= netResult.toFixed(2) %> € is real profit this month.
                        </div>
                    <% } %>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- EVENT PRICING & CAPACITY -->
        <div class="fin-card" style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <h2 style="margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 15px;">Event Pricing, Costs & Capacity</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                These are the defaults per kind of event. Every event inherits them, and a single event can
                override any value when you create it (e.g. a guest chef evening priced higher than the rest).
                Changing a number here immediately re-prices the history and the dashboard above.
            </p>
            <table class="fin-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Event Type</th>
                        <th class="num">Ticket Price</th>
                        <th class="num">Cost / Person</th>
                        <th class="num">Fixed Cost</th>
                        <th class="num">Max People</th>
                        <th class="num">IVA %</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit / Person</th>
                        <th class="num">Sold Out =</th>
                        <th></th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <% eventTypes.forEach(t => { %>
                        <%
                            // A <form> may not wrap <td>s, so the form lives in the last
                            // cell and the inputs join it via the HTML5 form="" attribute.
                            const fid = 'et-' + t.id;
                        %>
                        <tr>
                            <td>
                                <strong><%= t.name %></strong>
                                <% if (t.notes) { %><span class="sub"><%= t.notes %></span><% } %>
                            </td>
                            <td class="num"><input form="<%= fid %>" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="ticket_price" value="<%= t.ticket_price.toFixed(2) %>" required></td>
                            <td class="num"><input form="<%= fid %>" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="cost_per_person" value="<%= t.cost_per_person.toFixed(2) %>" required></td>
                            <td class="num"><input form="<%= fid %>" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" name="fixed_cost" value="<%= t.fixed_cost.toFixed(2) %>" required></td>
                            <td class="num"><input form="<%= fid %>" type="number" step="1" min="1" name="max_attendees" value="<%= t.max_attendees %>" required></td>
                            <td class="num"><input form="<%= fid %>" type="number" step="0.1" min="0" name="iva_pct" value="<%= (t.iva_rate * 100).toFixed(1) %>" required></td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <strong style="color: <%= t.profit_per_head >= 0 ? 'var(--secondary)' : 'var(--accent)' %>;"><%= money(t.profit_per_head) %></strong>
                                <span class="sub"><%= money(t.net_ticket) %> net - <%= money(t.cost_per_person) %></span>
                            </td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <strong style="color: <%= t.profit_at_capacity >= 0 ? 'var(--secondary)' : 'var(--accent)' %>;"><%= money(t.profit_at_capacity) %></strong>
                                <span class="sub">at <%= t.max_attendees %> people</span>
                            </td>
                            <td>
                                <form action="/admin/event-types" method="POST" id="<%= fid %>" style="margin: 0;">
                                    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="<%= t.id %>">
                                    <button type="submit">Save</button>
                                </form>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    <% }) %>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888;">
                "Sold Out =" is what one fully booked event of that type contributes to the shop:
                (net ticket - cost per person) x max people - fixed cost.
                Compare it against the <%= totalFixed.toFixed(2) %> € monthly burn to see how many events a month you need.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- SALES HISTORY -->
        <div class="fin-card" style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <h2 style="margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 15px;">Sales History per Month</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                Book profit = turnover minus <%= (plan.book_iva * 100).toFixed(0) %>% IVA, times the
                <%= (plan.book_margin_pct * 100).toFixed(0) %>% retail margin.
                Event profit uses each event's own price, IVA and cost structure from the table above:
                attendees x (net ticket - cost per person) - fixed cost.
                Events count in the month they take place in. Burn is that month's own fixed costs.
                <strong>Profit book shop = book profit + event profit - burn.</strong>
            </p>
            <table class="fin-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Month</th>
                        <th class="num">Sales Books</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Books</th>
                        <th class="num">Sales Event Tickets</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Events</th>
                        <th class="num">Monthly Burn</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Book Shop</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <% history.forEach(h => { %>
                        <tr>
                            <td><%= new Date(h.month).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) %></td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(h.bookSales) %></td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(h.bookProfit) %></td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <%= money(h.ticketSales) %>
                                <span class="sub"><%= h.tickets %> tickets / <%= h.events %> events</span>
                            </td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(h.eventProfit) %></td>
                            <td class="num muted">- <%= money(h.burn) %></td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <strong style="color: <%= h.shopProfit >= 0 ? 'var(--secondary)' : 'var(--accent)' %>;">
                                    <%= money(h.shopProfit) %>
                                </strong>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    <% }) %>
                    <% if (history.length === 0) { %>
                        <tr><td colspan="7" class="muted">No sales recorded in the last 12 months.</td></tr>
                    <% } %>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <h2 style="border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 15px;">Sales History per Year</h2>
            <table class="fin-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Year</th>
                        <th class="num">Sales Books</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Books</th>
                        <th class="num">Sales Event Tickets</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Events</th>
                        <th class="num">Burn</th>
                        <th class="num">Profit Book Shop</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <% yearly.forEach(y => { %>
                        <tr>
                            <td><%= y.year %><span class="sub"><%= y.months %> month<%= y.months === 1 ? '' : 's' %> with sales</span></td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(y.bookSales) %></td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(y.bookProfit) %></td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <%= money(y.ticketSales) %>
                                <span class="sub"><%= y.tickets %> tickets / <%= y.events %> events</span>
                            </td>
                            <td class="num"><%= money(y.eventProfit) %></td>
                            <td class="num muted">- <%= money(y.burn) %></td>
                            <td class="num">
                                <strong style="color: <%= y.shopProfit >= 0 ? 'var(--secondary)' : 'var(--accent)' %>;">
                                    <%= money(y.shopProfit) %>
                                </strong>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    <% }) %>
                    <% if (yearly.length === 0) { %>
                        <tr><td colspan="7" class="muted">No sales recorded yet.</td></tr>
                    <% } %>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #888;">* Years only cover the months shown above (rolling 12 months), not a full calendar year.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- STRATEGIC ANALYSIS -->
        <div class="fin-card">
            <h2 style="margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 15px;">Strategic Business Analysis: High Tide Community Model</h2>
            
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px;">
                <div>
                    <h4>1. Profit Structure</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                        <strong>Books:</strong> IVA is super-reduced at <%= (plan.book_iva * 100).toFixed(0) %>%, the retail margin is
                        <%= (plan.book_margin_pct * 100).toFixed(0) %>%. A <%= plan.avg_book_price.toFixed(2) %> € book therefore keeps
                        <%= plan.profit_per_book.toFixed(2) %> €.<br>
                        <strong>Events:</strong>
                        <% eventTypes.forEach(t => { %>
                            <%= t.name %> <%= money(t.profit_per_head) %>/head;
                        <% }) %>
                        Events have no stock risk, which is why they carry the staff costs.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4>2. Where the Burn Goes</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                        Staff plus their social security is
                        <strong><%= (((plan.helpers + plan.ss_helpers) / totalFixed) * 100).toFixed(0) %>%</strong>
                        of the <%= totalFixed.toFixed(2) %> € burn. Rent and utilities are only
                        <%= ((( plan.rent + plan.utilities) / totalFixed) * 100).toFixed(0) %>%, so opening hours - not the
                        premises - drive the cost base.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4>3. The "Hidden" Costs</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #cc0000;">
                        We have included <strong>Social Security (32%)</strong> for your helpers and your own <strong>Autónomo fee</strong>. Many small businesses fail because they only count the net salary.
                        Cooking events add a second hidden cost: the ingredients, which is why they have their own
                        <em>cost per person</em> above.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
